course: dictionary
lesson: 8735
title: Series: one thing after another
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A series is a group of things that come one after another, in a row. «Zara set her console to switch off at eight on its own and found a book series she loved instead.» A book series is a set of books about the same characters, and each book follows the one before.
explain: The word can mean different things, so the clues around it matter. «A tsunami is not one giant surfing wave: it is a series of huge waves» tells you there are many huge waves, not just one. In maths, a number series like 2, 4, 6, 8 is a row of numbers that follows a rule.
explain: Ask yourself: what is coming one after another here? A TV series is a set of programmes with the same story or people. In sport, a series is a set of games between the same teams. Check your meaning by swapping it in: «a set of waves» still makes sense, so you have it right.
fact: A series is a group of things that come one after another.
fact: «Van Gogh painted a series of sunflower paintings» means he painted a set of sunflower pictures, one after another.
fact: A number series is a row of numbers that follows a rule, such as 2, 4, 6, 8.
fact: In electricity, things in series are joined one after another in a single loop, so if one bulb breaks, all the bulbs go out.
fact: «Binge-watching a whole series» means watching a whole set of programmes with the same story or people.
exercise: «A life cycle is the series of changes a living thing goes through from birth to adult and new young.» What is a series here? | A single loud noise | A type of cloud | *A set of changes that happen one after another | A kind of living thing
exercise: What comes next in the number series 3, 6, 9, 12? | 13 | 11 | *15 | 18
exercise: In a circuit with bulbs in series, what happens if one bulb breaks? | The bulbs get brighter | Nothing changes | Only that bulb goes out | *All the bulbs go out
test: In «Zara found a book series she loved», what is a book series? | *A set of books with the same characters, one after another | A shop that sells books | A type of pencil case | A single book about a lost dog
test: «Van Gogh painted a series of sunflower paintings» means he painted | a sunflower that wilted and died | a garden of flowers with no pictures | one huge sunflower in a single picture | *a set of sunflower pictures, one after another
exam: Which means a series in sport? | A cup of water poured slowly | A goal kicked at the very end | A single race around a track | *A set of games between the same two teams
